---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REMOVAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/launch.ts";
---

<Base>
  <div class="max-w-xl mx-auto box-content px-gutter section-y">
    <h1 class="page-title text-ink mb-4">Code of conduct</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">Effective date: 25 September 2026.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      The Rupee Fund is a FOSS United community initiative run by community members. We adopt the
      conduct and anti-harassment standards of the{" "}
      <a
        href="https://fossunited.org/code-of-conduct"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-link">FOSS United Code of Conduct</a
      >, as reviewed on 7 September 2026, with the local rules below. Later changes to that source
      do not change this policy automatically. Where the source differs from the local rules, the
      local rules apply to the spaces of The Rupee Fund.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Scope and conduct</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      These standards apply to contributors, applicants, volunteers, and organisers in the spaces of
      The Rupee Fund and fund-related communications. Treat people with respect. Harassment,
      threats, discrimination, and disclosure of another person’s private information are not
      permitted.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Responsibility</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      The <a href="/team" class="inline-link">community team</a> is responsible for conduct in the spaces
      of The Rupee Fund. The Foundation contacts and event enforcement roles in the source policy are
      not assigned responsibilities in The Rupee Fund by this adoption. Foundation spaces remain subject
      to their own reporting procedures.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Report a concern</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
      To report a concern in a space of The Rupee Fund, email{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${REMOVAL_ADDRESS}`} class="inline-link">{REMOVAL_ADDRESS}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Attribution</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2">
      The adopted standards come from FOSS United. Its source credits the Major League Hacking
      policies under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence. This local adaptation
      uses the same <a
        href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-link">licence</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
